vision 3 rewrites the LES portion of the standard. The rev 2 language treated the Roache/Richardson grid)Tj 0 -12 TD (convergence index \(GCI\) as the default verification instrument for every solve regardless of turbulence treatment.)Tj T* (Two internal audits and a client peer review in Q1 2025 established that the treatment is technically incorrect for)Tj T* (large-eddy simulation and produces verification evidence that will not survive third-party scrutiny. The corrected)Tj T* (treatment is set out in Sections 4 and 5.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 406.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 50.5 TD (Nothing in this standard modifies the firm's Validation QA Procedure & Acceptance Criterion)Tj 0 -12 TD (\(Firm/QA/CFDME_Validation_Procedure_rev2\), the firm's Modeling Standards for Fire & Buoyant Flows)Tj 0 -24 TD (\(Firm/QA/CFDME_Units_SOP_rev2\). Where the requirements of this standard intersect those documents, all of them)Tj 0 -12 TD (apply concurrently.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 384.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 11.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD (2. Definitions)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 330.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 38.5 TD (Grid convergence index \(GCI\).)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( A quantitative estimator of numerical uncertainty attributable to spatial discretisation)Tj 0 -12 TD (error, computed from a monotonic sequence of solutions on systematically refined grids under an assumed observed)Tj T* (order of accuracy. Reported as a percentage band on a selected integrated quantity of interest. The GCI is defined)Tj T* (for solutions that converge to a unique grid-independent limit as the mesh is refined.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 288.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 26.5 TD (Plume resolution index \(D*/dx\).)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( The ratio of the characteristic plume diameter D* to the representative fire-region)Tj 0 -12 TD (cell edge length dx. D* is the buoyancy-driven length scale associated with a fire heat release rate Q_dot and is)Tj T* (defined as)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 270.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD <442a203d202820515f646f74202f20282072686f5f696e6620b720637020b720545f696e6620b72073717274286729202920295e7b322f357d>Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 228.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 26.5 TD (where rho_inf, cp and T_inf are the ambient density, specific heat and absolute temperature respectively, and g is)Tj 0 -12 TD (gravitational acceleration. The index D*/dx is the standard measure of how many cells span the buoyancy-dominated)Tj T* (length scale of a fire plume.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 186.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 26.5 TD (Resolved turbulent kinetic energy \(k_res\).)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( The turbulent kinetic energy carried by the explicitly resolved velocity)Tj 0 -12 TD (fluctuations in a large-eddy simulation, distinct from the sub-grid-scale contribution k_sgs modelled by the closure.)Tj T* (The resolved fraction is defined as k_res / \(k_res + k_sgs\).)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 132.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 38.5 TD (RANS and steady work.)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( In this document, "RANS and steady work" means Reynolds-averaged Navier-Stokes)Tj 0 -12 TD (simulations run to steady state, whether solved with a pseudo-time or true-steady solver, including internal buoyant)Tj T* (airflow of the type in the Copperline municipal HVAC envelope. Unsteady RANS \(URANS\) is treated as RANS for the)Tj T* (purposes of Section 4.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 102.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 14.5 TD (LES.)Tj/F1 9.5 Tf ( Large-eddy simulation, including the firm's reacting-fire LES stack \(fireFoam with EDC combustion and fvDOM)Tj 0 -12 TD (radiation\) and any non-reacting LES of atmospheric or building flow.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 80.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 11.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD (3. General Requirements for Verification)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 60 50.8 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 14.5 TD (Every deliverable that reports a CFD result shall contain a Verification section, plainly labelled as such, appearing in)Tj 0 -12 TD (the body of the report ahead of Validation and ahead of Results. The Verification section shall state, at minimum:)Tj ET Q Q
